        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on\nfor oral argument before the Supreme Court of the\nUnited States at 10:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GEN. NOEL J. FRANCISCO, Solicitor General,\nDepartment of Justice, Washington, D.C.,\nfor the United States, as amicus curiae,\nsupporting affirmance in 17-1618 and reversal in 17-1623."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Karlan --\nMs. Karlan, how do you answer the argument that\nback in 1964, this could not have been in\nCongress's mind because in -- in many states\nmale same-sex relations was a criminal offense;\nthe American Psychiatric Association labeled\nhomosexuality a -- a mental illness?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you do with the argument that this is a\nnon-discriminatory policy because it applies\nequally to relationships between women and\nrelationships between men? In other words, your\nfriends on the -- or -- or you emphasize that\nyou need to know the sex of the individuals\ninvolved before you can determine whether or not\nthere's a violation and that that brings it within\nTitle VII."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. KARLAN",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KARLAN: No more than what you did in Oncale. No more than what you did in Price Waterhouse. No more than what you did in --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me. Can I understand your argument in context? Let's answer the question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well counselor --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you drawing a distinction between the literal meaning of \"because of sex\" and the ordinary meaning of \"because of sex\"? And, if so, how are we supposed to think about ordinary meaning in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The issue is not whether Congress can or should prohibit employment discrimination because of sexual orientation. The issue, rather, is whether it did so when it prohibited discrimination because of sex. It did not for two reasons. First, sex means whether you're male or female, not whether you're gay or straight. So if you treat all gay and men -- gay men and women exactly the same regardless of their sex, you're not discriminating against them because of their sex."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But what if the decision maker makes a decision based on sexual orientation but does not know the biological sex of the person involved?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Well, there is no reported case that does that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What if it happened? We have had a lot of hypotheticals of things that may or may not have happened. What if that happens? Is that discrimination on the basis of sex where the decision maker doesn't even know the person's sex?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "document_hash": "70cb9f2786ce69439dc0bb422fbbf8b8fc0e06144f0607915b0033198201607c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-70cb9f2786ce-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "And in 1964, if you look at the members of Congress's brief, they will tell you if you looked in the dictionary there was no phrase \"sexual orientation.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1618",
